  "worked_solution": "Remember that $sec$  is the reciprocal of $cos,$  $csc$ is the reciprocal of $sin$  and $cot$  is the reciprocal of $tan.$\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sec}⁡{60}^{∘}=\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡{60}^{∘}},\\,\\operatorname{csc}⁡{30}^{∘}=\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡{30}^{∘}},\\,\\operatorname{cot}⁡{30}^{∘}=\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{tan}⁡{30}^{∘}}.\n$$\n\nThe angle ${60}^{∘}$ and ${30}^{∘}$ are special, and its trigonometric ratios have the values\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡{60}^{∘}=\\frac{1}{2},\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡{30}^{∘}=\\frac{1}{2},\\,\\operatorname{tan}⁡{30}^{∘}=\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6\\operatorname{sec}⁡{60}^{∘}+3\\operatorname{csc}⁡{30}^{∘}+\\operatorname{cot}⁡{30}^{∘} & = \\\\ 6(\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡{60}^{∘}})+3(\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡{30}^{∘}})+\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{tan}⁡{30}^{∘}} & = \\\\ \\frac{6}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡{60}^{∘}}+\\frac{3}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡{30}^{∘}}+\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{tan}⁡{30}^{∘}} & = \\\\ \\frac{6}{(\\frac{1}{2})}+\\frac{3}{(\\frac{1}{2})}+\\frac{1}{(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3})} & = \\\\ 12+6+\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{3}} & = \\\\ 18+\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{3}} & = \\\\ 18+\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{3}}\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{\\sqrt{3}} & = \\\\ 18+\\sqrt{3}. & \\end{aligned}\n$$",
